  "_contested": [
    "primitives/Curl noise — left as source because it is consumed like a noise function, but it is really ∇× applied to a potential field, so arguably an operator.",
    "primitives/Poisson disk sampling — source, because it makes points from a seed and a density. But 'Circle, rectangle & Apollonian packing' in art2d is a generator, because there the packing image is the artefact. Same machinery, different framing.",
    "geometry3d/Signed distance fields — called a source, but SDFs are really a representation. This is the strongest argument for a fourth tier.",
    "levels/maze algorithms — recursive backtracker, Prim's, Wilson's, Eller's are named after methods but produce mazes, which are artefacts. Left as generators. 'Braid, unicursal & weave mazes' is an operator because it modifies an existing maze.",
    "textures/Full PBR map sets — an output format rather than a source, operator or generator. Fits none of the three cleanly.",
    "bizops — nearly everything is a solver over supplied data. By the naming test a roster is an artefact, so generator. The thing that actually separates these from a dungeon generator is input class, not tier.",
    "biomed/patient-specific implants, sockets, crowns, insoles — left as generators, but every one requires a scan. Again: input class, not tier."
  ]
}
